etting the  right prices in the right place at the  right time  as you can imagine speed was really the  key here right how do we do that in the  most effective way  to really take us to where we needed to  be  so as we went through understood these  challenges  these are really foundational to trying  to determine what's the right technology  that we choose and you know my hat's off  to  our product management organization and  working with our business partners to  really outline these challenges in a way  that our technology teams  could really take these and determine  what is the right  technology solution that we need in  order to enable this and when you look  at the complexity of the business  you know with our prices as mentioned  before  this this is a difficult task that we  had in front of us and  uh we were you know really diving in to  understand these challenges and figure  out  how do we move forward uh to solving  them  in the most effective way it's a very  interesting use case  so let me ask you this why did you  choose google cloud  as a platform for this solution yeah you  know our our team uh  really stepped back when we were looking  at again these use cases and the  challenges that we had in front of us  and we went through an evaluation  of various technologies and one thing  that  is really part of our culture is we go  through  proof of concepts and in this case  we actually ran uh two things in  parallel we were  looking at all open source technology  and then we were looking at uh some of  the components within google cloud  to really kind of test this out and see  how does the technology really help us  to solve the business problem and in the  most you know  effective way and so the teams  did this very rapidly went through these  proof of concepts  and you know this is uh just culturally  what we do  as an organization to ensure that what  we're selecting is the most effective  and so we ended up selecting google  cloud and and really  three main reasons that i'll describe  here of  of why we did that first you got to  think about  having the right architecture that  enabled flexibility  was key behind this and when you take a  something like pricing which is a very  very critical component to your retail  business  and looking at how you scale that we  need the right architecture and  flexibility  to enable us to do that that was that  was number one  number two you know leveraging some of  google's managed services like  spanner and pub sub was another key  element to this and  you know one of the things that when we  look at our engineering team we want to  make sure that  we're building and delivering new  capabilities for the business  as much as possible and by leveraging  spanner pub sub you know we didn't have  to spend a lot of time on and worry  about having to upgrade the underlying  technology you know to to support the  the overall solution so it really  enabled our engineers to focus on  building out these capabilities and  driving value for the business which is  what we want  the third thing i'll call out is around  some of the  you know analytics and by having our  data in a more  centralized location and solution  we're able to get a lot more valuable  insights into  just how we're performing and where we  at in the life cycle and so  that that was really uh the third area  that  was key for us and understanding that  performance  and how we take immediate action is  really what  helped us to make that decision and  google was really  uh you know key to helping us get there  as soon as possible  so again i'll just say hats off to  our engineering teams and and the google  team you know partnering together  uh to get us uh uh to to this point and  helping us  as we made this selection to really uh  move us forward in the most  uh effective why  all right so you heard from ron on the  use case and the pain points  now let's discuss the solution that was  built to solve this  so t