nefit  of true time and what that means is that  easily lets you add a globally  consistent timestamp  for all of your events so the benefit  for the solution is that  this establishes a ground truth of the  order of  all of your messages for all time this  means that you can make downstream  assumptions  anchored on that ground tooth which  solves a lot of complexity for dependent  systems  and services up next are the event-based  triggers  that pull this data into the messaging  queue from  cloud spanner and our messaging queue is  cloud pub sub  so this is the layer where the records  are filtered and written  to a centralized messaging queue pops up  and the benefit of this is that the  multiple subscribers can be registered  to get data from this messaging  publishing queue one of the main  subscribers  is the master publish view the data  or the events are loaded to a  corresponding low latency database  or materialized view for easy query  access  this has to be like a really low latency  database so think of it like an  in-memory database or a really low  latency  nosql database it just depends on the  size of the database  we've actually tested this pattern for  millions of records  and millions of products and this holds  pretty well and one of the main reasons  why we're able to do that  is because we are able to separate the  writes from the reads in parallel you  also have the archiver  which writes these events to a global  archive called the cloud storage  in a compressed state and then  corresponding to the archiver is a  replayer  so replayer then reads the records in  order of the long-term storage  and then decompresses them and loads  them into a new club club stream so if  you ever need to go back  and look how the events were loaded into  the system how you got certain data  was a chronological order of all the  events you're able to easily do that  with the  replayer and lastly we also have the  ability to make  one-off price changes using the price ui  this price ui goes through the  centralized api  and writes the information into cloud  spanner and once the information is in  cloud spanner it goes through the same  process  of pushing the data to master publish  view and to the archiver that we just  discussed  so hopefully this gives you an overview  of the solution that was created to  solve this use case  all right so let's move on to the  benefits of the solution  saron let me ask you this now that the  solution is live  can you please hear some of the benefits  that you've seen so far  absolutely you know the the first thing  uh  that we accomplished was really getting  that centralized view of all the  key components for pricing for all  channels and  as i mentioned earlier guys that was one  of the the challenges we had of just  trying to manage this across multiple  systems and  getting that single view uh was  absolutely key to us  and and achieving that benefit the  second  is increasing our speed to market for  you know the price changes and enabling  just  a lot more efficiencies for how we're  making those changes  you know again you go across multiple  systems  it takes a lot of time takes a lot of  coordination and getting us centralized  improves our speed to market so we can  do that much more effectively  and then a third that i'll call out is  really around the ability to be  proactive and  you know just managing our price changes  and you know knowing that our price  changes have been executed  as you can imagine our store associates  you know they're dealing with a lot uh  in the stores just making sure they're  serving customers so when  we're thinking about the pricing and how  we sent our prices down to stores to  execute we want that to be  as efficient as possible and one of the  key benefits here is it's made us a lot  more effective with how we  you know prioritize those changes and  and how much we're sending  down to our stores so that they can be  more effective at  implementing the necessary prices that  we actually need so  just a tremendous uh progress here and  uh definitely  you know getting a lot of benefit out of  the capabilities that have been put in  place  so now that you're getting all these  benefits ron what are your plans for  the new features and functionalities  that you are looking to add to the  solution as we move forward  yeah you know we're going to spend some  time uh you know focused on  uh really these these three main areas  i'll walk through first is  uh around our price performance and  some of our price change analytics you  know when we look at the  number of price changes and how those  prices are performing in the markets you  know how our customers are responding  that's one area that we want to continue  to build out  and enhance more for the overall  solution  the second area is around price  governance and  some of the audit capabilities again  i'll reflect back to  some of the complexities we had with  multiple systems  and you know how do we have the right  visibility the  number of users that can make changes to  our prices you know it was very complex  and  very difficult to manage and so this  foundation we have in place now  is really positioned as well so that we  can  more effectively track and and control  how those prices are are handled so  we'll continue to enhance that  functionality  as we move forward and then the third  area that i would call out just around  you know price testing and measurement  and you know how we put  our prices in market and getting the  results back  and and measuring the effectiveness of  that is absolutely key and  uh we'll we'll leverage this foundation  in place to build upon  so that we get more effective  measurement and understand how we're  progressing  going forward so ultimately we want to  ensure that we're  you know putting forward the the best  price you know for our customers  at the right time at the right channel  and uh the foundation we now have in  place  is uh going to be key to helping us  continue that  priority in that journey all right so as  you heard from ron  this pattern provides many important  benefits over traditional architecture  so the first one is a global consistency  so cloud spanner has the benefit of true  time so it  easily lets you add a globally  consistent timestamp for each of your  events  so this establishes a ground truth of  the order for all of your messages at  all time  and you can have your downstream systems  work with that assumption  which is a huge benefit and solves a lot  of complexity for those downstream  systems  the next one is high availability  so multi-region rights are necessary for  systems that run in multiple places  east or west you know disaster recovery  but multi-region  rights are also great for sending events  from a single system in the data center  to multiple systems that run in the  stores  in this example or vice versa so for  things like price  inventory tracking real-time sales  metrics  this is uh important to have high  availability across the board  and as you mentioned earlier we've  actually tested this solution  for millions and millions of products  across channel  and the solution holds pretty well so if  you have some  very stringent slas and you want to make  sure that the performance doesn't  degrade when you're using millions of  millions of record then  this solution is probably the right one  for you and then as ron mentioned  earlier as well  is um this lets you focus  on these strategic tasks and the dev  teams  are focused on building business logic  or the business value directly  associated with the use case  and not worry about some of the  operational tasks of keeping the servers  up scaling them up or down because the  system takes care of that  this results in quicker time to market  and much lower total cost of ownership  for the solution  i want to again thank ron baker vice  president of merchandising technology at  lowe's companies  for sharing the information and his  thoughts with us  and to you uh thank you for listening to  our presentation  hope you found the content useful i just  want to say  add to that vikas uh you know thanks for  the partnership here with  google and you know really appreciate  the opportunity to speak  to what we've been able to accomplish  here in the pricing area you know like i  mentioned  uh an introduction you know lowe's  advancing our business  with technology like never before and  i'm excited to see  so many capabilities like pricing you  know enabled and proud of what our teams  have been able to accomplish  with this modern technology so i hope  all of you  as well got some valuable insights into  the content  and i want to thank all of you for your  time today

